  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental funds (General, Street, CDBG) from p5 Total Governmental Funds column; beginning_cash/ending_cash are the fund balances the statement rolls forward (282,405 -> 385,521). These are fund balances, not cash: governmental cash and investments on the p4 balance sheet total 388,200, less payroll withholding liabilities of 2,679 = 385,521 (CDs 153,216 are inside that, so ending_investments is left null). Business-type = Water, Sewer, Trash from p7 total column; Sales 212,793 (water, sewer and trash fund sales) is category Utility Charges (attempt 3, user rule 2026-10-28); operating expenses by cost type with function utilities; nonoperating principal/interest/loan fees treated as disbursements; roll-forward on net position (402,725 + 214,351 - 171,408 = 445,668). Governmental 'Charges for services' 625 (p5) is licenses and permits per the p11 General Fund schedule (attempt 3). Business-type reported totals are sums of printed operating and nonoperating lines (no single total printed), marked computed. Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): the governmental funds balance sheet (p4) totals (assets 388,200, liabilities 2,679, fund balance 385,521) equal the government-wide governmental column (p1), so governmental lines come from p4 Total Governmental Funds with fund balance by classification (restricted 463 + 153,763, assigned 9,893, unassigned 221,402); business-type lines and the printed totals from the p1 Statement of Net Position. General Fund detail is the p11 combining schedule (more detailed than the p9 budget schedule, so p9 not double counted; p9 budget_final attached only to lines that map one-to-one); p9 matches p11 totals. Street fund from p10 (Motor vehicle and Other income lines have no actual, budget only, so not recorded). The 'Intergovernmental' receipt line holds state assistance and rural fire contract money (p11, p10); no homestead/pro-rate breakdown is printed. No budget schedules for Water, Sewer or Trash funds in the trimmed PDF, so no business-type detail lines. Cash-flow statement (p8) not used (cash basis, proprietary null). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
